// What PowerShell says to the shared scope rules: a variable exists from its first assignment in
// the function, script block or script that holds it, and a block sees the names around it. Names
// are the words that start with `$` (or `@`, a splat) and a read is any such word; a name with a
// scope or drive qualifier (`$script:x`, `$env:x`) is none of these. Format: core_semantics::scopes::rows.
names Word
bare
methods ScriptBlock Program
// A function that reads `$PSBoundParameters` may hand every parameter on.
dynamic psboundparameters
conventions null erroractionpreference warningpreference verbosepreference debugpreference informationpreference progresspreference confirmpreference whatifpreference
Program var-scope
Function var-scope
ScriptBlock var-scope
ParamDecl declares=value|parameter token=first/declare
AssignStmt token=first/assign."=" implicit=value|let@unseen
